{
	title: 'Parallel tool results sit under their calls',
	spec: 'In the terminal, a batch of parallel tool calls shows each result right under its own call, as one card, as web cards do; each call streams under its own header and keeps its output when done. Exception (terminal only; the web has no immutable scrollback): when the calls, each counted as a header and 5 output rows, would not fit on one screen, calls and results stay separate blocks and each result links to its call (#<call>), so a finishing call never rewrites scrollback and forces a full redraw. Display order only (frame.order); the transcript keeps arrival order. Background bash output arrives later as its own block. Invariant restored: three parallel inspect calls showed three headers, then three detached results.',
